{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% from "_macros.j2" import todo, or_todo, mailto %}
{% block title %}Privacy notice · {{ b.brand }}{% endblock %}
{% block main %}
<div class="wrap narrow prose">
  <h1>Privacy notice</h1>
  <p class="meta">Last updated {{ today.strftime("%d %B %Y") }}</p>

  <div class="callout">
    <strong>In short:</strong> we tell care consultancies about care services that may need their help, using
    information from the public CQC and Companies House registers. If you'd rather not be included, email
    {{ mailto(b, "Opt out", b.email or "us") }} and we'll remove you for good. <a href="opt-out.html">How to opt out</a>.
  </div>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>{{ b.brand }} is run by {{ or_todo(b.legal_name, "your legal name") }}{% if b.company_number %}, company number
    {{ b.company_number }}{% endif %}, {{ or_todo(b.address, "your postal address") }}. We are the controller of the
    personal data described here. Contact us at {{ mailto(b, "Privacy question", b.email or "our email address") }}{% if b.phone %}
    or {{ b.phone }}{% endif %}.{% if b.ico_registration %} We are registered with the Information Commissioner's Office
    (registration {{ b.ico_registration }}).{% endif %}</p>

  <h2>Whose information this is about</h2>
  <p>Mostly organisations: care providers and companies. Some care providers are <strong>sole traders or
    partnerships</strong>, whose business name, address and phone number identify a person. This notice is mainly for
    them. It also covers people who contact us, and our customers' contacts.</p>

  <h2>What we collect, and where from</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>From the Care Quality Commission</strong> (its public register and API): service and provider names,
      addresses, phone numbers, websites, the type of care provided, registration dates and inspection ratings.</li>
    <li><strong>From Companies House</strong> (its public register): company names, numbers, registered office
      addresses, company type and activity (SIC) codes.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>We do <strong>not</strong> collect the names of registered managers, nominated individuals or company directors:
    these are removed before anything is stored. We collect no special category data. Ratings concern services, not
    individuals.</p>

  <h2>What we use it for</h2>
  <p>To identify care services and companies that may need CQC compliance support, such as those that have just
    registered, received a poor rating or been newly set up, and to tell our customers about them. Our customers are
    CQC compliance consultancies, who may contact the services we list to offer their help.</p>

  <h2>Our lawful basis</h2>
  <p>Legitimate interests (UK GDPR Article 6(1)(f)): ours in running this service, and our customers' in offering
    relevant services to care providers. The information is already published on public registers for transparency,
    we use only what is needed, and anyone can opt out at any time. We have assessed this balance and keep a written
    record of it.</p>

  <h2>Who receives it</h2>
  <p>Our subscribing customers, who receive a weekly list for the areas they cover. They decide how they use it, and
    are responsible for their own marketing, including the Privacy and Electronic Communications Regulations. We label
    every lead with the contact rule that applies (for example, sole traders may not be sent unsolicited marketing
    emails), and require customers to pass on any opt-out requests to us. Our computer and email providers process
    data for us under contract. We don't sell data to anyone else.</p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>Twelve months. Older records, lists and reports are deleted automatically each week. If you opt out, we keep only
    your identifier (for example your CQC ID or company number) on a suppression list, so that you are never added
    again.</p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>You can ask us to stop using your information (<strong>object</strong>), to delete it, to correct it, or for a
    copy of it. To opt out of our lists, see <a href="opt-out.html">how to opt out</a>. For anything else, email
    {{ mailto(b, "Data protection request", b.email or "us") }}. We reply within one month. If you're unhappy with how we
    handle your information, you can complain to the Information Commissioner's Office at
    <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/">ico.org.uk</a>.</p>

  <h2>Automated decisions and transfers</h2>
  <p>We don't make decisions about you that have legal or similarly significant effects by automated means. We sort
    public register entries into lists; people decide whether to contact anyone. Your information is stored in the UK.
    Where a supplier stores data outside the UK, we make sure appropriate safeguards are in place.</p>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>This website uses no cookies and no tracking.</p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>We will update this notice if anything changes, and show the date above.</p>
</div>
{% endblock %}
